TI  - Pleural Endosalpingiosis: A Novel Entity.
PG  - e137-e139
LID - S0012-3692(25)04974-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2025.07.4067 [doi]
AB  - Endosalpingiosis, defined as ectopic fallopian tube tissue, is a rare entity 
      usually found in the intraabdominal cavity. We present a case of pleural 
      endosalpingiosis presenting as an exudative pleural effusion diagnosed through 
      pleural biopsy and histologic examination. To our knowledge, no case reports in 
      the literature have described this process occurring in the pleural cavity. This 
      report highlights this novel entity and the diagnostic dilemma it poses.
