TI  - A 14-Year-Old Boy With Severe Dyspnea After Coughing Up a Bitter-Tasting Fluid.
PG  - e99-e102
LID - S0012-3692(25)05509-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2025.10.005 [doi]
AB  - A 14-year-old boy with no significant medical history presented to the emergency 
      department with a sudden onset of debilitating left-sided chest pain and severe 
      dyspnea. The symptoms began acutely while he was at rest, approximately 1 hour 
      before arrival. During a coughing fit, he expectorated a small amount of clear, 
      watery, and distinctly bitter-tasting fluid. His medical background was 
      unremarkable, with no history of prior respiratory symptoms, asthma, smoking, 
      recent trauma, or chronic illnesses. The patient lives in a rural village, has no 
      travel history, and has no special dietary habits that would predispose him to a 
      different diagnosis.
