TI  - A 2-Month-Old Boy With Respiratory Distress, Thrombocytopenia, and an Aggressive 
      Mediastinal Mass.
PG  - e135-e141
LID - S0012-3692(25)05675-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2025.11.006 [doi]
AB  - A 2-month-old male infant with symptoms of dyspnea and progressive 
      thrombocytopenia was referred to our tertiary care center. Physical examination 
      at the referring hospital revealed tachypnea, head-nodding respiration, and poor 
      appetite. Laboratory tests revealed severe thrombocytopenia (platelet count, 11 × 
      10(9)/L), anemia (hemoglobin, 73 g/L), and coagulopathy (thrombin time, 33.9 s; 
      fibrinogen: 0.25 g/L; D-dimer: 55.13 mg/L). Echocardiography revealed pericardial 
      effusion and decreased ventricular function. He was initially diagnosed at the 
      referring hospital with "severe pneumonia and thrombocytopenia" and received 
      empirical treatment with antibiotics and platelet and red cell transfusions but 
      showed limited clinical improvement.
