PG  - e11-e15
LID - S0012-3692(25)04978-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2025.07.4069 [doi]
AB  - A 74-year-old woman sought treatment with a 4-day history of high fever and 
      rapidly progressive dyspnea. A 2-day course of ceftriaxone and betamethasone 
      administered in an outpatient setting did not result in any clinical improvement, 
      leading to her admission to our hospital. She demonstrated a slight cough but did 
      not report heartburn, night sweats, hemoptysis, myalgia, arthralgia, or weight 
      loss. Her family history was unremarkable.
