TI  - A 71-Year-Old Man With Gas Accumulation in the Left Atrium.
PG  - e75-e81
LID - S0012-3692(24)05300-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2024.10.004 [doi]
AB  - A 71-year-old man with a history of atrial fibrillation presented to the 
      emergency department with sudden unconsciousness after finishing lunch. Just 
      4 weeks ago, the patient underwent radiofrequency ablation for atrial 
      fibrillation and regularly took rivaroxaban for anticoagulant therapy. According 
      to the medical history, the patient suffered recurrent chest tightness and 
      heartburn after radiofrequency ablation without other discomforts. During 
      transportation to the hospital, the patient experienced a drop in BP after 
      forceful vomiting.
