TI  - A Febrile 67-Year-Old Man With Pulmonary Consolidation and Contralateral Nodules.
PG  - e119-e125
LID - S0012-3692(24)05299-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2024.10.003 [doi]
AB  - A 67-year-old man who currently smoked (45 pack-years) was referred to the 
      emergency department for fever and exacerbation of cough over the last week. The 
      current illness began 1 month earlier with nonproductive cough and exertional 
      dyspnea. He did not report anorexia, hemoptysis, or weight loss. Outpatient 
      treatment with cefditoren and moxifloxacin did not improve his symptoms. No 
      remarkable medical history was reported. The patient was admitted for further 
      evaluation.
